  "name": "EDF Sport 70",
  "author": "whirligig",
  "version": "1",
  "notes": "A 70 mm ducted-fan sport jet on six cells. The fan is the SAME rotor machinery as the trainer's propeller \u2014 eleven short, wide blades turning fast in a shroud \u2014 and the only thing that makes it a ducted fan is the `duct` entry. That one field says the wake cannot contract, which is worth about a quarter more static thrust than an open fan of the same disc area and power, and it tells the blade model to stop taking a tip loss, because a shroud is exactly a device for stopping air escaping round the blade tips. The duct is also why an EDF is so poor at low speed and so good at high: all that thrust comes from a small disc, so the jet is fast and the static efficiency is bad, but it keeps working long after a propeller has run out of pitch. Datum is the wing quarter chord.",
